This fork of `rars` is licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0.

See LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE beside this file for the two texts.
Either may be chosen, at your option.

## Why this file no longer says WTFPL

Upstream https://github.com/bitplane/rars states its licence two ways,
and they disagree with each other:

  * its repo-root COPYING says "WTFPL licensed with 1 extra clause /
    1. don't blame me / It's all yours, including all the blame";
  * its workspace Cargo.toml declares `license = "MIT OR Apache-2.0"`,
    and every version published to crates.io (0.9.0 through 0.9.3 as of
    26 Aug 2026) carries that same MIT OR Apache-2.0 metadata.

Upstream ships no MIT or Apache-2.0 text of its own - COPYING and
README.md are the only such files in its root - so GitHub's own licence
detector reports the repository as "Other / NOASSERTION".

Earlier vendoring copied upstream's COPYING verbatim while our
Cargo.toml carried upstream's OTHER answer, so this directory asserted
both at once. That is now settled in one direction: WTFPL explicitly
permits relicensing, and MIT OR Apache-2.0 is what the upstream author
himself declares and publishes, so this fork states it, ships both
texts, and is classifiable by SPDX tooling.

The original work is bitplane's. The fork carries substantial
modifications made for nzbfast; upstream is credited above and in
COPYRIGHT.md, and the vendoring policy is in VENDORING.md.
